<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Patch>
  <!--
    ==========================================================================
    HumanTemperatureBand_Ashkarr.xml        Jawa_Patches - authored 2026-08-23
    ==========================================================================

    The XENOTYPE third of NORMALIZE_TEMPERATURE_TOLERANCES_1. Plants shipped as
    PlantTolerances_Ashkarr.xml (577) and animals as AnimalTolerances_Ashkarr.xml
    (456). This is people.

    OWNER'S RULING, 2026-08-23, asked with the numbers in front of him:
    GEAR REQUIRED AT THE EXTREMES. Not "survivable everywhere" - temperature is
    what makes the nightside hostile and the dayside lethal, and a world where
    everything survives everywhere has no climate.

    ==========================================================================
    THE MECHANISM, and why this is ONE operation and not sixty-nine
    ==========================================================================

    A XenotypeDef is a LIST OF GENE NAMES and nothing else. Tolerance is the
    StatDef ComfyTemperatureMin/Max (StatDefOf.cs:56), fed by GeneDef statOffsets
    in StatWorker.GetValueUnfinalized (StatWorker.cs:184-207).

    MEASURED 2026-08-23: 35 of our 69 species carry a temperature gene and
    34 CARRY NONE AT ALL. Patching genes reaches at most half of them. Patching
    the base stat reaches every humanlike in the game, and - the point - it
    leaves every existing gene offset intact as RELATIVE flavour. Jawa stay the
    heat-hardy ones, Chiss stay the cold-hardy ones; the whole distribution just
    moves. That is also the precedent plants and animals already set: both were
    normalized by moving the BASE field, never by adding modifiers.

    ==========================================================================
    THE NUMBERS
    ==========================================================================

    SafeTemperatureRange is comfy +/-10 (GenTemperature.cs:86), and SAFE is the
    number that matters - it is the hypothermia/heatstroke boundary. So:

        comfy -40 .. +45   =>   safe -50 .. +55

    Against Ash'karr's real ground, MEASURED across all 21,872 tiles:

        BMT_CrystalCaverns  -62.4   NEEDS GEAR
        AB_PropaneLakes     -59.8   NEEDS GEAR
        HorrorWastes        -49.3   survives
        AB_RockyCrags       -45.3   survives
        ExtremeDesert med   +48.2   survives
        AB_MechanoidIntr    +62.5   NEEDS GEAR
        ExtremeDesert peak  +66.1   NEEDS GEAR
        coldest ground      -82.0   NEEDS GEAR

    Four extremes demand clothing and shelter; the rest of the planet is
    livable. That is the ruling, expressed as a number.

    Vanilla shipped 16..26 (safe 6..36), which left every one of our species
    88.0 C short of the coldest ground and 30.1 C short of the hottest.

    ==========================================================================
    CONSEQUENCES, accepted deliberately rather than discovered
    ==========================================================================

    * This patches a VANILLA CORE def, so it moves EVERY humanlike - our 69
      species, vanilla xenotypes, and every NPC faction including raiders.
      That is correct for a shared planet: the enemy lives here too.
    * Gene offsets STACK on top. A species with MinTemp_LargeDecrease (-20)
      lands at comfy -60 / safe -70. Alpha Genes' AG_ColdImmunity (-273) and
      Outland's -999 still make their carriers immune, as intended.
    * Jawa carry a heat gene, so they end up able to work the dayside peak
      their own biome reaches. That is the right species to have that property.

    NOT wrapped in a PatchOperationConditional, DELIBERATELY, and
    validate_patch.py warns about it every run. The target is Core, which
    cannot be absent - the only way this stops matching is Ludeon renaming the
    stat in a game update, and there a RED ERROR is exactly what we want.
    Wrapped, every pawn on the planet would quietly revert to 6..36 and the
    first sign would be colonists dying of cold in a biome we had signed off.
    A patch that matches nothing logs nothing; that is the failure this
    project keeps paying for. Same reasoning as JawaWorld_Name.xml.
    ==========================================================================
  -->

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Human"]/statBases/ComfyTemperatureMin</xpath>
    <value><ComfyTemperatureMin>-40</ComfyTemperatureMin></value>
  </Operation>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Human"]/statBases/ComfyTemperatureMax</xpath>
    <value><ComfyTemperatureMax>45</ComfyTemperatureMax></value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
